# What must never enter the image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so this file is the only thing standing
# between the build context and a container that carries the operator's
# credentials. Two of these matter more than the rest:
#
#   .env      the Gemini key, the Flask session secret, the Firebase web key
#   *.json    the Firebase service account private key lives in one of these,
#             and it grants full administrative access to the project
#
# A container image is not a secret. Anyone who can pull it can read every
# layer, including files a later layer deleted.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Service account keys and everything else that ends in .json. The two the
# application genuinely reads at runtime are allowed back in below.
*.json
!firebase.json
!firestore.indexes.json
!database.rules.json

# Local environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# The benchmark corpus: hundreds of generated pages and their manifests. Used
# to measure conversion quality during development, never at runtime.
bench/

# The logo masters and the script that derives the served assets. The derived
# assets in static/img/ are what the pages reference and they do ship; these
# are the multi-megabyte originals.
brand/

# Generated results from local runs. The container makes its own in /tmp.
uploads/
public/

# Node, used only to build static/css/app.css. The built stylesheet is
# committed and is what ships.
node_modules/
tailwind.config.js
tools/
static/css/tailwind.src.css

# Documentation and tests. Keeping them out is about image size and about not
# publishing internal notes, not about them being unimportant.
*.md
tests/

# Local logs and OS clutter
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Development tooling that must never enter the image.
package.json
package-lock.json
